    "statement": "theorem centerColumn_not_isEventuallyPeriodic_of_white_times\n    (h : ∀ p > 0, ∀ N : ℕ, (∀ t ≥ N, centerColumn (t + p) = centerColumn t) →\n        ∀ t ≥ N, centerColumn t = false → evolve (t + p) 1 = evolve t 1) :\n    ¬ IsEventuallyPeriodic centerColumn := by\n  sorry",
    "reason": "A SUFFICIENT CONDITION FOR PRIZE 1, IN THE SHAPE THE WALL ASKS FOR: to prove that the centre column never repeats it is enough to control column 1 at the WHITE times of a hypothetically periodic centre column. Everything else is already pinned. Why it is true: split the times past the onset by the colour of the centre cell. At a black time, column -1 repeats for free (centerColumn_succ_of_black at t and t + p, the black-times lemma of this tier). At a white time, column_one_of_white says column 1 is the xor of the next centre cell with column -1, so the hypothesis plus the centre column's own period makes column -1 repeat there too. Column -1 is then eventually periodic and so is column 0, which not_isEventuallyPeriodic_adjacent at i = -1 forbids. WHY A PROOF OF THE WALL WOULD CITE IT: it is the model centerColumn_other_of_cohomologous_column in a second coordinate, and it converts the wall from a statement about an existential over all columns into a statement about ONE named column at a NAMED SUBSET of times. PROVED IN SCRATCH: explorer/seeder_scratch_p1c.lean, axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. By column_one_of_white the hypothesis is interchangeable with the same statement about column -1 at white times, which is exactly the negation of the open node centerColumn_periodic_damage_white; the two are one object seen from either side of the origin.",
    "disclaims": "IT IS NOT THE WALL AND IT DOES NOT WEAKEN IT. What it buys is a smaller target, not an easier one: nothing here says the residual (column 1 at the white times) is any more tractable than P1, and I claim no evidence that it is. The hypothesis is a conditional whose antecedent is the negation of P1, so it is unsatisfiable in fact, no p and N can be exhibited, and the node carries NO WITNESS by design rather than by omission. Anyone who proves the hypothesis has proved Prize 1, which is the point and also the warning.",
